{
 "_about": "Real photographs for Photo Expedition's field guide. tools/fetch-expedition-photos.mjs searches Wikimedia Commons for FEATURED pictures (the community's best photographs, all free to use) — first inside the subject's own categories (cats, searched with deepcat:), then by search terms — and only accepts a picture whose title, description or categories match one of the `must` patterns, so a search for 'monal' can never come back with a fencing trophy. It saves the photos into games/photo-expedition/photos/ and writes photos/manifest.js with the photographer credit and licence for every one. Run by .github/workflows/fetch-expedition-photos.yml. Patterns in `must` are matched against the picture's title, object name and categories only (never the free-text description, which mentions all sorts); `also` patterns must match the whole text too. Entries are fetched in order and no picture is used twice, so the site landscapes come last. `not` patterns reject a picture (used to keep animals out of the landscape heroes, and flowers out of the baobab). `alsoStrong` patterns must match the title/categories (the landscape heroes need a landscape word there, so an albatross over an island is not a landscape).",
 "width": 1100,
